      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "Doctor, it is her nose and eyes. Since the beginning of the month she sneezes and sneezes, every morning, and her eyes are red and itchy.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:36",
      "end_timestamp": "00:52",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]",
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Aditi, do your eyes feel itchy?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:53",
      "end_timestamp": "00:57",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Very itchy. And my nose.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:59",
      "end_timestamp": "01:02",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "When is it worst, indoors or outdoors?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:04",
      "end_timestamp": "01:08",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "Outdoors, in the garden, and when we go to school in the morning. By afternoon she is better, and at night nearly normal.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:11",
      "end_timestamp": "01:23",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Is there a cough or any wheezing, any trouble in the chest?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:25",
      "end_timestamp": "01:32",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]",
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "No cough, no wheeze. Her chest is fine, thank God.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:33",
      "end_timestamp": "01:39",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]",
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Does Aditi take any medicines, or have any allergies to medicines or foods?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:41",
      "end_timestamp": "01:48",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "No allergies to anything. And no regular medicines.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:51",
      "end_timestamp": "01:55",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any other conditions, like eczema or asthma?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:56",
      "end_timestamp": "02:00",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "A little eczema on the elbows when she was small, but it has gone now.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:02",
      "end_timestamp": "02:10",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Does anyone else in the family have hay fever?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:12",
      "end_timestamp": "02:18",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, me, I'm her mother, I get it every spring. And her father too, a little.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:20",
      "end_timestamp": "02:27",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Temperature 36.6, and I'll listen to your chest too, Aditi. Breathe in and out.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:08",
      "end_timestamp": "03:16",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Her chest is clear. I'd say this pattern, sneezing, itchy red eyes, worse outdoors, with a family history, is most likely hay fever.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:22",
      "end_timestamp": "03:36",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'm going to start Aditi on cetirizine, 5 mg once a day, in the morning, which helps the sneezing and itching.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:58",
      "end_timestamp": "04:10",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, the liquid is easiest. I'm also going to start a nasal spray, fluticasone, 50 micrograms, one spray in each nostril once a day.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:15",
      "end_timestamp": "04:30",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Wash her face and change her clothes when she comes in from outside, keep bedroom windows closed in the morning, and rinse her eyes with cool water.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:02",
      "end_timestamp": "05:18",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
